 Top trading ideas by experts on November 2, 2026 
 Experts recommended top 6 trading ideas on November 2 including
 HCL Technologies, Titan Company
 Persistent Systems, Adani Ports
 Did our AI summary help? 
 Market Mastery
The benchmark indices extended their gains for another session, with the Nifty 50 rising half a percent on October 30 despite weak market breadth. On the NSE, around 2,383 stocks declined against 881 advancing stocks. While the market may extend its upward momentum in the near term, the sustainability of these gains will be crucial to watch. Here are some short-term trading ideas for investors to consider:
 Hitesh Rathi, Technical Analyst (Equity & Derivatives) at Angel One 
HCL Technologies has signalled a potential trend reversal, indicated by a consolidation breakout on its daily charts. A golden crossover of its 20EMA, above its 200 DSMA, indicates towards strong tailwinds of momentum in the short term.
At the same time, a super pattern bullish breakout on its Point and figure chart, potentially underscore the bullish undertone. On its smaller time frame 0.5% Renko charts, the stock has triggered a bullish swing breakout, offering a risk adjusted opportunity in a sharply trending stock. Buying is recommended around Rs 1,428-1,425.
 Samvardhana Motherson International | CMP: Rs 156.5 
Samvardhana Motherson International has a confluence of support at the Rs 150-148 band, marked by the lows of a bullish anchor column on its P&F charts, and a prior price breakout on its Candlestick charts. This presence of demand in this zone, is validated by the multiple bullish formations from the same price zone, like the bullish 100% pole and weak breakout, indicating that strong demand continues to remain present at lower levels.
A weak breakout on the 1% Renko charts, further validates the presence of strong demand at lower levels. Alongside this, the repeated formation of long wicks on daily candlestick charts, indicates a potential selling exhaustion. Buying is recommended at around Rs 155-154.
 Dixon Technologies (India) | CMP: Rs 11,000 
A bearish crossover of the 20 DEMA, over its 200 DSMA, following a bearish crossover of the 20 EMA, below its 50 EMA, has made the short-term trend convincing bearish. A follow through Double bottom sell, of an bearish anchor column, indicates a potential resumption of the bearish trend in Dixon Technologies.
On the Renko charts as well, a pull back to the upper channel of the Donchian channel and a follow through swing break down, provides further confirmation of the bearish trend. Hence, the selling is recommended in the stock around Rs 11,010-11,000.
 Jatin Gedia, Technical Research Analyst, VP, Derivatives & Technical Research at Teji Mandi 
Titan was in a short term downtrend. It has completed a five wave decline and has started its pullback forming higher highs and higher lows on the daily charts. On the weekly charts, it has formed an Engulfing bull candlestick pattern which is a trend reversal pattern.
Positive divergence and a bullish crossover on the momentum indicator suggest a buy signal. We expect the stock to retrace toward Rs 4,582 - 4,697 which are the 38.2% and 50% Fibonacci retracement levels of the Rs 5,187 to Rs 4,209 decline.
Persistent Systems was consolidating within a narrowing range for the past couple of weeks. It has broken out of that consolidation to the upside. Breakout has been accompanied by above-average volume suggesting a genuine breakout and indicating the resumption of the primary uptrend.
A bullish crossover on the momentum indicator across monthly, weekly and daily time frames suggests a buy signal. Thus, considering the price volume breakout and the momentum setup, the stock is expected to rise toward Rs 6,595, which is the 100% Fibonacci extension level of the previous wave.
 Adani Ports and Special Economic Zone | CMP: Rs 1,850 
Adani Ports has been in a long term uptrend. On the daily charts, it has broken out of a bullish flag pattern suggesting resumption of the next leg of the uptrend. In the previous trading session, the stock dipped towards the 20-hour moving average (Rs 1,820) and witnessed buying interest.
The daily momentum indicator has a positive crossover; therefore, this dip towards the support level should be considered a buying opportunity. We expect the stock to rise towards Rs 1,933 which is the 100% Fibonacci extension level of the previous wave.
