 Nifty Trading Plan for November 2, 2026 
 Nifty could extend gains for third consecutive session and move above 23,175
 Decisive move above 23,175 could take index towards 23,500
 On downside, immediate support is placed at 22,800, followed by 22,650
 Did our AI summary help? 
 Market Mastery
With momentum indicators showing further improvement and the Nifty 50 holding firmly above its short-term moving averages, both of which are sloping upwards, the index could extend its gains for a third consecutive session and move above the immediate resistance zone of 23,150-23,200 (near October swing high of 23,175). A decisive move above this range could take the index towards 23,500, which is likely to act as a crucial hurdle. On the downside, immediate support is placed at 22,800, followed by 22,650. Meanwhile, if the Bank Nifty manages to defend Friday's low, a rally towards the 55,000-55,100 resistance zone cannot be ruled out. The next upside levels to watch would be 55,650 and 56,100. However, a break below Friday's low could expose the index to further downside towards 54,000, according to market experts.
On October 30, the Nifty 50 surged 116 points, or 0.51 percent, to close at 23,053, while the Bank Nifty declined 223 points, or 0.41 percent, to settle at 54,687. Market breadth turned negative, with 2,383 stocks declining against 881 advancing on the NSE.
 Jatin Gedia, Technical Research Analyst, VP, Derivatives & Technical Research at Teji Mandi 
Nifty held the support zone of 22,400 - 22,500 and rallied more than 700 points to close above the 23,000 mark. On the monthly and weekly charts, it respected and closed above the 40-month exponential moving average (22,803) and the rising support trendline derived by joining the previous swing lows of 21,743 and 22,182 respectively. Holding on to crucial support zones despite global headwinds indicates bullish sentiment.
The previous swing high and the 38.2 percent retracement level of the previous three months decline from 24,774 to 22,180 is placed at 23,170. We expect Nifty to break through this resistance and head higher toward 23,477, which is the 50% retracement level of the decline from 24,774 to 22,180. Support base shifts higher from 22,500 to 22,680. Daily and hourly momentum setups are in sync, with a positive crossover supporting the bullish price action.
On the derivatives front, maximum Call Open interest is placed at 23,500 while maximum Put open interest is placed at 22,000 followed by 22,500. Put strikes at 22,800 to 23,000 added open interest (indicating support) while Call writers unwound their positions across the same strikes, resulting in the PCR (Put Call ratio) rising from 1.41 to 1.61. Considering the technical setup and the derivatives data, we expect the positive momentum in Nifty to continue towards 23,400 - 23,500 with 22,800 - 22,680 as the support base.
 Strategy : Buy Nifty November Futures at around 23,053, with a stop-loss of 22,950, and target of 23,514.
 Hitesh Rathi, Technical Analyst (Equity & Derivatives) at Angel One 
On a weekly basis, Nifty continues to remain range-bound, extending its sideways trajectory for the fifth consecutive week. The sharp rebound witnessed last week from the 22,500–22,400 band reinforces the presence of strong demand at lower levels and highlights the significance of the rising trendline on the weekly chart, which has repeatedly acted as a sacrosanct support.
Furthermore, the considerable improvement in overall market breadth and sentiment has helped ease concerns among market participants. That said, stiff overhead resistance continues to make the path to higher levels challenging.
Going forward, unless the index delivers a convincing breakout above the 23,150–23,200 band, caution remains warranted, with a conscious effort to avoid chasing upward momentum. A decisive breakout above this resistance band would mark the formation of the first higher high–higher low structure on the daily chart, signalling a potential shift in the short-term trend. A weekly close above this crucial zone would further confirm the breakout on the weekly timeframe.
In terms of levels, immediate support for the index is now likely to be found at the 22,950-22,900 band, followed by a stronger cushion at the 22,800 level. On the flipside, 23,100-23,160 band is an immediate hurdle, followed by a stronger resistance at the 23,400-23,450 band.
 Strategy : Buy Nifty Futures near 22,850, with a stop-loss of 22,750 and book profits near 23,000-23,100.
